H2("Consequences for choosing a modern model");
P("The best model differs between wound datasets: {{sel.best.med}} on Medetec, {{sel.best.co2}} on CO2Wounds-V2, {{sel.best.fus}} on FUSeg and {{sel.best.azh}} on AZH (seed averages), and with single-seed models the best architecture changes with the seed on {{sel.bestchange.n}} of the four datasets. Choosing on one wound dataset and deploying on another loses {{sel.off}} Dice on average over the {{n.ord}} ordered pairs (at most {{sel.off.max}}), against {{sel.rand}} for a random choice (Table 5); the paired difference is {{rv.sel.diff}} ({{rv.sel.diff.ci}}). For comparison, choosing on one random half of a wound dataset and deploying on the other half loses {{rv.sel.half}}. With single trained models instead of seed averages the chooser did about as well as a random pick: {{sel.s0.off}}, {{sel.s1.off}} and {{sel.s2.off}} against {{sel.s0.rand}}, {{sel.s1.rand}} and {{sel.s2.rand}} with the seed-{{d.seed0}}, seed-{{d.seed1}} and seed-{{d.seed2}} models.", { after: 100 });
